data: {"text":"1. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in FIR No. 78/2026 dated 01.04.2026,"}

data: {"text":" registered at Police Station Lalpur, under Sections 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, and seeks"}

data: {"text":" regular bail in the aforesaid case.\n\n2. That the present case arises out of a property dispute between the"}

data: {"text":" Complainant and the Applicant's family. The Applicant submits that he has been falsely implicated in the said FIR with mal"}

data: {"text":"icious intent and ulterior motives to settle the ongoing property dispute.\n\n3. That the Applicant was not present at the spot at the time of the alleged incident and"}

data: {"text":" has CCTV evidence from a nearby shop establishing his presence elsewhere at the material time. The Applicant was arrested on 02.04.2026 and has been languishing in judicial custody since then without any just"}

data: {"text":"ifiable cause.\n\n4. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in the present case due to the property dispute with"}

data: {"text":" the Complainant. The allegations leveled against the Applicant are baseless and fabricated, and the same have been made"}

data: {"text":" with the sole intention of harassing the Applicant and"}

data: {"text":" his family members.\n\n5. That the Applicant is a law-abiding citizen with deep roots in the community and has no intention or"}

data: {"text":" inclination to flee from justice. He has full faith in the judicial system and is"}

data: {"text":" ready to face the trial and cooperate with the investigation in all resp"}

data: {"text":"ects.\n\n6. That the Applicant has no criminal antecedents whatsoever and has never been involved in any criminal activity in the past. He"}

data: {"text":" is a person of good character and reputation in society and has always conducted himself in"}

data: {"text":" accordance with law.\n\n7. That the Applicant is ready and willing to cooperate with the investigating"}

data: {"text":" agency and shall make himself available whenever required during the course of investigation. He undert"}

data: {"text":"akes to appear before the Court as and when directed and shall not tamper with evidence or influence"}

data: {"text":" witnesses.\n\n8. That the continued detention of the Applicant in judicial custody is violative of his fundamental right to personal liberty as guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India,"}

data: {"text":" especially when the investigation can be completed without keeping him behind bars.\n\n9. That while"}

data: {"text":" Section 303 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 is classified as non-bailable, the present"}

data: {"text":" case warrants the grant of bail considering the circumstances of false implication, availability of corroborative evidence establishing the Applicant's innoc"}

data: {"text":"ence, and the fact that the Applicant poses no flight risk.\n\n10. That the Applicant undertakes to abide by such terms and conditions as this"}

data: {"text":" Hon'ble Court may deem fit to impose while granting bail and shall not"}

data: {"text":" misuse the liberty granted to him in any manner whatsoever."}

