data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"cause_title","type":"template","content":"IN THE COURT OF DISTRICT & SESSIONS JUDGE\n\nCriminal Miscellaneous Case No. _____ of 2026\n\nIN THE MATTER OF:\n\nAmit Kumar Sahu\nS/o Shri Birendra Sahu\nAge: 28 years\nR/o House No. 14, Harmu Housing Colony, Ranchi - 834002\n                                              ... Applicant\n\nVersus\n\nState of Jharkhand through the District Magistrate / S.P., Ranchi\n                                              ... Opposite Party","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"application_heading","type":"template","content":"APPLICATION FOR Regular Bail UNDER SECTION 480 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"addressing_clause","type":"template","content":"TO,\nTHE HONOURABLE DISTRICT & SESSIONS JUDGE,\nRanchi\n\nMOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in FIR No. 78/2026 dated 01.04.2026, registered at Police Station Lalpur, under Sections 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, and seeks regular bail in the aforesaid case.\n\n2. That the present case arises out of a property dispute between the Complainant and the Applicant's family. The Applicant submits that he has been falsely implicated in the said FIR with malicious intent and ulterior motives to settle the ongoing property dispute.\n\n3. That the Applicant was not present at the spot at the time of the alleged incident and has CCTV evidence from a nearby shop establishing his presence elsewhere at the material time. The Applicant was arrested on 02.04.2026 and has been languishing in judicial custody since then without any justifiable cause.\n\n4. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in the present case due to the property dispute with the Complainant. The allegations leveled against the Applicant are baseless and fabricated, and the same have been made with the sole intention of harassing the Applicant and his family members.\n\n5. That the Applicant is a law-abiding citizen with deep roots in the community and has no intention or inclination to flee from justice. He has full faith in the judicial system and is ready to face the trial and cooperate with the investigation in all respects.\n\n6. That the Applicant has no criminal antecedents whatsoever and has never been involved in any criminal activity in the past. He is a person of good character and reputation in society and has always conducted himself in accordance with law.\n\n7. That the Applicant is ready and willing to cooperate with the investigating agency and shall make himself available whenever required during the course of investigation. He undertakes to appear before the Court as and when directed and shall not tamper with evidence or influence witnesses.\n\n8. That the continued detention of the Applicant in judicial custody is violative of his fundamental right to personal liberty as guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India, especially when the investigation can be completed without keeping him behind bars.\n\n9. That while Section 303 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 is classified as non-bailable, the present case warrants the grant of bail considering the circumstances of false implication, availability of corroborative evidence establishing the Applicant's innocence, and the fact that the Applicant poses no flight risk.\n\n10. That the Applicant undertakes to abide by such terms and conditions as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit to impose while granting bail and shall not misuse the liberty granted to him in any manner whatsoever."},{"section_id":"prayer","type":"template","content":"PRAYER\n\nIt is, therefore, most humbly prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:\n\na) Grant Regular Bail to the Applicant, Amit Kumar Sahu, in connection with FIR No. 78/2026 dated 01.04.2026, PS Lalpur, under Section 480 of BNSS, 2023, on such terms and conditions as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit;\n\nb) Pass such other orders as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case, in the interest of justice.\n\nAnd for this act of kindness, the applicant shall ever pray.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"verification","type":"template","content":"VERIFICATION\n\nI, Amit Kumar Sahu, the Applicant herein above named, do hereby verify that the contents of the above application are true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief and nothing material has been concealed therefrom.\n\nVerified at Ranchi on this _____ day of _________, 2026.\n\nDEPONENT\n\n\n_________________________\nAmit Kumar Sahu\n(Applicant)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"advocate_block","type":"template","content":"THROUGH:\n\n_________________________\nSmoke Test\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. ____________________\n\nPlace: Ranchi\nDate: 06 May 2026","alignment":"right"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

